      <reaction compartment="compartment_5460" fast="false" id="reaction_5696004" metaid="metaid_147" name="ACSF2 ligates CoA-SH to MCFA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <html:p>Acyl-coenzyme A synthetases (ACSs) catalyse the activation of fatty acids by thioesterification to CoA, the fundamental initial reaction in fatty acid metabolism. Mitochondrial acyl-CoA synthetase family member 2 (ACSF2) preferentially ligates CoA-SH to medium-chain fatty acids (MCFA), around C8 in length (Watkins et al. 2007).</html:p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF>
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="#metaid_147">
              <dc:creator>
                <rdf:Bag>
                  <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                    <vCard:N rdf:parseType="Resource">
                      <vCard:Family>Jassal</vCard:Family>
                      <vCard:Given>Bijay</vCard:Given>
                    </vCard:N>
                    <vCard:ORG rdf:parseType="Resource">
