      <reaction compartment="compartment_5460" fast="false" id="reaction_5695989" metaid="metaid_150" name="ACAD11 dehydrogenates BH-CoA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <html:p>Acyl-CoA dehydrogenase family member 11 (ACAD11) is a mitochondrial membrane-bound enzyme that can catalyse the alpha, beta-dehydrogenation of acyl-CoA esters. ACAD11 shows highest expression in the brain and is shown to dehydrogenate the C22 acyl-CoA behenoyl-CoA (BH-CoA) to 2,3-dehydrobehenoyl-CoA (DBH-CoA) (He et al. 2011).</html:p>
        </notes>
