      <reaction compartment="compartment_17957" fast="false" id="reaction_8848246" metaid="metaid_152" name="DBI, ACBD7 bind MCFA-CoA and LCFA-CoA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <html:p>Acyl-CoA-binding protein (DBI, aka ACBP) can bind medium- and long-chain acyl-CoA esters (MCFA-CoA, LCFA-CoA) with very high affinity. It is localised to the ER (and Golgi) and may function as an intracellular carrier of acyl-CoA esters (Hansen et al. 2008, Bloksgaard et al. 2014). Acyl-CoA-binding domain-containing protein 7 (ACBD7) shares around 60% sequence homology with DBI and is proposed to also bind fatty acyl-CoAs but its function is yet to be determined.</html:p>
        </notes>
